Search-Dense Summary – product.category (Product Category)
Core Purpose (1-line functional):
Hierarchical classification system for organizing all products and services, used for reporting, searching, accounting, and access control.
Key Functional Use Cases:

Build multi-level product trees (e.g. Electronics > Phones > Smartphones)
Default accounting (income/expense accounts, taxes)
Filter products in sales, purchase, and inventory
Costing method and inventory valuation settings (per category)
Website e-commerce category mapping
Reporting (sales by category, stock value by category)
Permission and visibility control

Technical DNA:

Model Type: models.Model (persistent + mail.thread)
Key Fields:
name (char, required), complete_name (computed)
parent_id → product.category (hierarchical)
child_id (One2many)
property_account_income_id, property_account_expense_id → account.account
property_cost_method, property_valuation
property_stock_valuation_account_id, property_stock_account_input, property_stock_account_output
removal_strategy_id, route_ids

Critical Hooks: _compute_complete_name, onchange_parent_id, _check_category_recursion
Security: product.group_product_manager + company rules

RAG Routing Keywords:
product category, product categories, item category, goods category, stock category, accounting category, product hierarchy, category structure, product group, merchandise category, pos category, e-commerce category
Related Models (most joined):

product.product / product.template (via categ_id)
product.category (parent/child)
account.account (income/expense/valuation)
stock.warehouse, stock.location
pos.category (separate but often mapped)

Ultra-Dense Vector Paragraph:
product.category is Odoo’s hierarchical model for classifying products with parent_id, complete_name, property accounts (income/expense), valuation method, and stock accounts. It drives product organization, default accounting behavior, inventory costing, reporting, and is the main categorization system referenced by every product.template, sales, purchase, and stock operations across Odoo.